## Quick Reference: Lesson 006

### XOR A Instruction

| Instruction | Operation | T-states | Bytes | Flags |
|-------------|-----------|----------|-------|-------|
| XOR A | A ← A XOR A (= 0) | 4 | 1 | S,Z,P set; H,N,C cleared |
| LD A,0 | A ← 0 | 7 | 2 | No flags affected |

**Comparison:** XOR A is 43% faster, half the size, and sets flags

### 16-Bit Counter Pattern

```asm
LD BC,count          ; Load 16-bit counter
Loop:
    ; Work here
    DEC BC           ; Decrement counter
    LD A,B
    OR C             ; Check if zero
    JR NZ,Loop       ; Continue if not zero
```

### Screen Memory

| Property | Value | Hex | Notes |
|----------|-------|-----|-------|
| Start | 16384 | $4000 | First bitmap byte |
| End | 22527 | $57FF | Last bitmap byte |
| Size | 6144 | $1800 | Total bytes |
| Attributes start | 22528 | $5800 | Colour data |
| Attributes size | 768 | $0300 | 32×24 bytes |

### Instructions Used

| Instruction | Purpose | T-states | Bytes |
|-------------|---------|----------|-------|
| XOR A | Set A=0 | 4 | 1 |
| LD BC,nn | Load 16-bit counter | 10 | 3 |
| DEC BC | Decrement BC | 6 | 1 |
| OR C | Logical OR (check zero) | 4 | 1 |
| PUSH AF | Save A and flags | 11 | 1 |
| POP AF | Restore A and flags | 10 | 1 |
| INC H | Add 256 to HL | 4 | 1 |

### Performance Comparison

| Operation | Assembly | BASIC | Advantage |
|-----------|----------|-------|-----------|
| Clear screen | ~114ms | ~14s | ~125× faster |
| Set A=0 | 4 T-states | ~1000 T-states | ~250× faster |
| 6144 iterations | ~400k T-states | ~50M T-states | ~125× faster |

